/**
 * Server-Sent Events variant of the chat endpoint. Emits a sequence of typed events over `text/event-stream`. This endpoint is NOT auto-generated by Orval — SSE responses cannot be represented in standard OpenAPI. Use the handwritten `useAiChatStream` hook exported from `@workspace/api-client-react` instead.
 * The boundary between the generated client and this hand-written hook is intentional and documented. Do not move this endpoint into the generated surface without first confirming Orval supports SSE. See PR-06.
 * Event shapes — each SSE frame is `data: <JSON>\n\n`:
 *
 *   { "type": "stage", "stage": "building-context" | "calling-model" | "streaming" }
 *     — Phase transition; update the UI progress indicator.
 *
 *   { "type": "delta", "delta": "<token>" }
 *     — Incremental model token for real-time streaming display.
 *     Accumulate deltas until the "done" event to reconstruct the full response.
 *
 *    { "type": "session_started", "sessionId": "...", "title": "...", "updatedAt": "..." }
 *      — The server reserved the conversation before model work starts. Persist this
 *        session identity immediately; the final "done" event carries the saved messages.
 *
 *    { "type": "execution_started", "executionId": "...", "status": "running",
 *      "resumeToken": "..." | undefined, "resumable": true }
 *      — Durable execution identity. Store the executionId and resumeToken outside
 *      the conversation content. An SSE disconnect is not cancellation; use the
 *      execution status endpoint and explicitly resume with the token after a
 *      server restart. The token is only returned on the initial claim.
 *
 *    { "type": "plan_activity", "stage": "understand" | "scope" | "plan" | "execute" | "validate",
 *      "status": "active" | "done" | "info", "stepTitle"?: "...",
 *      "action"?: "inspect" | "create" | "modify" | "delete" | "test" | "configure",
 *      "files"?: ["..."], "resultSummary"?: "...", "nextStepTitle"?: "...",
 *      "approvalRequired"?: true, "approvalReason"?: "..." }
 *      — Safe implementation-plan progress. File names are the approved
 *      relative scope only; source contents, runtime roots, fingerprints,
 *      execution IDs, and provider diagnostics are never included.
 *
 *    { "type": "execution_nodes", "executionId": "...", "nodes": [
 *      { "id": "...", "title": "...", "status": "queued" | "running" | "passed" | "failed" | "blocked",
 *        "allowedFiles": ["..."], "dependencies": ["..."],
 *        "validationProfile": "...", "attempts": 0 }
 *    ] }
 *      — Bounded server-owned execution tree snapshot for Mission Control.
 *        File paths and node metadata are exposed for progress visibility;
 *        source contents are never included. The same snapshot is stored in
 *        the durable execution checkpoint.
 *
 *    { "type": "done", "sessionId": "...", "message": { "id": "...", "role": "assistant",
 *       "content": "...", "sources": "...", "toolTrace": "...", "createdAt": "...",
 *       "outcome": "SUCCEEDED" | "FAILED" | "INTERRUPTED",
 *       "failureKind": "QUALITY_REVIEW" | "TOOL_FAILURE" | "CANCELLATION" | "RECOVERY_FAILURE" | "INCOMPLETE" | undefined,
 *       "retryable": true | false, "recoveryState": "NONE" | "REQUIRED" | "INCOMPLETE",
 *       "forensicDiagnostic": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ForensicDiagnostic" } | null }, "sources": [...],
 *     "pendingChanges": [{ "path": "...", "absolutePath": "...", "newContent": "...",
 *      "originalContent": "..." | null, "reason": "...", "validationProfile": "..." }],
 *       "proposalId": "..." | undefined, "proposalUnavailable": "..." | undefined,
 *      "taskResult": { "kind": "CODE_EXTRACTION_RESULT", "extractedCode": "..." }
 *        | { "kind": "BEHAVIOR_ANSWER_RESULT", "answer": { ... } }
 *        | { "kind": "FINDING_RESULT", "finding": { ... } }
 *        | { "kind": "FORENSIC_REPORT_RESULT", "report": "...", "evidence": [...] }
 *        | { "kind": "WORKSPACE_REVIEW_RESULT", "report": "...", "evidence": [...] }
 *        | { "kind": "REPAIR_RESULT", "phases": [...], "readiness": "READY" | "BLOCKED" | "NOT_PROVEN" }
 *        | undefined,
 *      "execution": { "iterations": 24, "maxIterations": 24, "toolCalls": 35,
 *      "prefetchToolCalls": 8, "loopToolCalls": 27,
 *      "stopReason": "iteration_budget" | "provider_timeout", "synthesisStarted": true,
 *      "recoveryStarted": false,
 *       "diagnosticCodes": ["FORENSIC_CONTRACT_RECOVERY_REJECTED"],
 *       "diagnosticDetails": ["Evidence Map: missing current source record"] } }
 *     — Final assembled response. sources is a string[] of referenced file paths.
 *       taskResult is a discriminated union keyed on `kind` (one of CODE_EXTRACTION_RESULT,
 *        BEHAVIOR_ANSWER_RESULT, FINDING_RESULT, FORENSIC_REPORT_RESULT, WORKSPACE_REVIEW_RESULT, REPAIR_RESULT);
 *       absent for generic chat turns. Narrow on `kind` before accessing task-specific fields.
 *       The persisted toolTrace JSON may include `forensic_status` entries with
 *       `isFixtureLocal: true` when the proven Finding is supported only by
 *       fixture/test/spec evidence (not production source). Such entries also carry
 *       `productionReachability: "NOT_PROVEN"` and `repairReadiness: "BLOCKED"`.
 *       Repair execution is blocked when isFixtureLocal is true — caller and
 *       input-path evidence from non-fixture production source is required.
 *        Forensic audit completions include the same bounded
 *        forensicDiagnostic projection in the done message and persisted
 *        history. ANALYSIS_INCOMPLETE includes one allowlisted reason,
 *        bounded unread/truncated scope, and exactly one next action;
 *        NO_VERIFIED_FINDING is emitted only after complete reconciled coverage.
 *
 *    { "type": "error", "code": "...", "message": "...", "executionId"?: "...",
 *       "sessionId"?: "...", "outcome"?: "FAILED" | "INTERRUPTED",
 *       "failureKind"?: "QUALITY_REVIEW" | "TOOL_FAILURE" | "CANCELLATION" | "RECOVERY_FAILURE" | "INCOMPLETE",
 *       "quality"?: { "code": "QUALITY_REVIEW_LOW", "score": 0.42, "threshold": 0.78, "reasons": ["bounded reason"] },
 *       "retryable"?: true | false, "recoveryState"?: "NONE" | "REQUIRED" | "INCOMPLETE",
 *       "forensicDiagnostic"?: { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ForensicDiagnostic" },
 *       "hint"?: "..." }
 *     — Terminal error; the stream will close after this event.
 *
 *   { "type": "execution_guard", "code": "REPEATED_TOOL_CALL", "tool": "...",
 *     "message": "..." }
 *     — Deterministic Repair Plan safety stop after repeated identical tool calls.
 *
 *    { "type": "tool_call", "tool": "...", "args": { "...": "..." }, "cached": false }
 *      — A tool invocation started by the agent.
 *
 *    { "type": "tool_result", "tool": "...", "source"?: "...", "cached": false }
 *      — A tool invocation completed; source is a bounded file label when available.
 *
 *     { "type": "repair_state",
 *       "state": "VALIDATING" | "REPAIRING" | "READY_FOR_REVIEW" | "BLOCKED",
 *       "detail"?: "..." }
 *       — Named state of the approval-gated Verified Repair Loop. VALIDATING
 *       means a registered profile is running; REPAIRING means a failed
 *       validation still has bounded correction attempts remaining;
 *       READY_FOR_REVIEW means validation passed while changes remain pending;
 *       BLOCKED means validation was unavailable, exhausted, or otherwise
 *       cannot establish a safe repair.
 *
 *      { "type": "validation",
 *        "validation": { "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ValidationResult" },
 *        "repairState": "VALIDATING" | "REPAIRING" | "READY_FOR_REVIEW" | "BLOCKED",
 *        "attempt": 1, "maxAttempts": 3 }
 *        — Structured server-owned validation evidence. Every result carries
 *        a stable evidenceId, observedAt timestamp, and artifactRef. A passed
 *        result without all three evidence fields is not proof and must remain
 *        blocked by approval gates. The command and registered profile are
 *        bounded by the server; arbitrary commands are not accepted.
 *
 *     { "type": "model_call" }
 *       — Bounded progress metadata indicating that a model response was received.
 *         Provider and model routing identifiers are server-side diagnostics.
 *
 *     { "type": "production_trace", "status": "PROVEN" | "NOT_PROVEN" | "OUT_OF_SCOPE",
 *       "nodes": [...], "edges": [...] }
 *       — Runtime-observed route/orchestrator/provider/output provenance. It is
 *         PROVEN only when every supplied link has runtime evidence.
 *
 *     { "type": "cross_file_trace", "status": "PROVEN" | "NOT_PROVEN" | "OUT_OF_SCOPE",
 *       "maxDepth": 1, "nodes": [...], "edges": [...] }
 *       — Bounded graph-grounded provenance for explicit file scope. Edges may
 *         include an exact sourceSpan with file, line, column, and snippet.
 *
 *     { "type": "evidence_integrity",
 *      "code": "TELEMETRY_CONSISTENT" | "TELEMETRY_INCONSISTENT",
 *      "consistent": true | false, "violations": ["bounded content-free reason"],
 *      "readAttempts"?: 12, "uniqueFilesRead"?: 8, "evidenceFileCount"?: 6,
 *       "acceptedEvidenceCount"?: 4,
 *       "evidenceSourceCoverage"?: {
 *         "status": "COMPLETE" | "PARTIAL" | "NONE",
 *         "requestedFiles"?: ["src/a.ts", "src/b.ts"],
 *         "roots": [...]
 *       } }
 *      — EI-011/012 run-ledger telemetry reconciliation. consistent=false means
 *        the verdict failed closed on TELEMETRY_INCONSISTENT; violations are
 *         bounded, content-free reason labels (never source contents). For a
 *         file-scoped audit, requestedFiles is the ordered canonical manifest
 *         and must match the forensic_status manifest and per-file root coverage.
 *
 *    { "type": "decision_trace",
 *      "taskType": "BEHAVIOR_QUERY", "evidenceSelected": 1, "validator": "behavior-answer",
 *      "recoveryAttempt": 0, "recoveryFailureKind"?: "...",
 *      "finalState": "VERIFIED" | "NOT_PROVEN" | "RECOVERY_REQUIRED" | "FAILED",
 *      "rejectionReason": ["..."],
 *      "verdictScope"?: "PRODUCTION" | "FIXTURE_LOCAL" | "TEST_LOCAL" | "SPEC_LOCAL" | "MIXED" | "NOT_PROVEN",
 *      "scopedFindingStatus"?: "PRODUCTION_PROVEN" | "FIXTURE_PROVEN" | "TEST_PROVEN" | "MIXED_EVIDENCE" | "NOT_PROVEN" }
 *      — Task-router trace emitted live as the verdict is decided. Carries
 *        the verdict's proof scope so a watcher sees whether the proven
 *        Finding is fixture-local before the report lands.
 *
 *    { "type": "thinking", "iter": 1, "max": 28 }
 *      — Agent loop progress metadata.
 *
 *    { "type": "synthesis_start", "iter": 20, "max": 24 }
 *      — The final no-tool synthesis window started; subsequent tool calls
 *        are rejected and the model must write from gathered evidence.
 *
 *    { "type": "execution_diagnostic",
 *      "code": "FORENSIC_CONTRACT_RECOVERY_REJECTED" | "FORENSIC_CONTRACT_RECOVERY_PARSE_FAILED" |
 *        "FORENSIC_CONTRACT_RECOVERY_FAILED" | "EXECUTION_RESPONSE_FORMAT_INVALID" |
 *        "EXECUTION_JSON_CORRECTION_FAILED" | "EXECUTION_JSON_CORRECTION_RETRY_FAILED" |
 *        "EXECUTION_PROVIDER_FAILURE" | "EXECUTION_NO_EDIT_TOOL",
 *       "details"?: ["bounded contract violation"] }
 *        — Bounded execution/recovery metadata; details are optional,
 *        limited failure labels/codes, and are not report content or evidence.
 *
 *    { "type": "intent",
 *      "intent": "CHAT" | "PROJECT_QUERY" | "FORENSIC_AUDIT" | "DELIVERY",
 *      "operationMode": "CHAT" | "FORENSIC_AUDIT" | "DELIVERY",
 *      "requiresEvidence": true | false }
 *      — Server-authoritative routing decision for this turn.
 *
 *    { "type": "audit_state",
 *      "sourceCoverage": "COMPLETE" | "PARTIAL" | "NONE",
 *      "behaviorAssessment": "COMPLETE" | "INCOMPLETE" | "NOT_STARTED",
 *      "findingStatus": "PROVEN" | "NO_FINDING" | "NOT_PROVEN",
 *      "repairReadiness": "READY" | "BLOCKED",
 *      "productionReachability": "PROVEN" | "NOT_PROVEN" | "OUT_OF_SCOPE" }
 *      — Bounded forensic ledger state; it contains no source content.
 *
 *    { "type": "verification",
 *      "stage": "MODEL_RESPONSE" | "VERIFIED_RESPONSE",
 *      "responseLength": 123,
 *      "sourceCount": 1,
 *      "evidenceCount": 1,
 *      "acceptedEvidenceCount": 1,
 *      "rejectionReasons": ["bounded reason"] }
 *      — Bounded response/evidence verification telemetry.
 *
 *    { "type": "stream_reset" }
 *      — The provider stream broke and the server switched to a buffered fallback.
 *
 * The full TypeScript event union is exported as `AiStreamEvent` from `@workspace/api-client-react`. Treat that type definition as the authoritative schema — it must stay in sync with this description.
 *
 *    The `done` event may also include `toolTrace`,
 *   `operationMode: "FORENSIC_AUDIT" | "DELIVERY" | "CHAT"` — the
 *   read-only audit mode must not be rendered as a missing Plan/Apply/Commit/Push
 *   delivery trace,
 *   `telemetry: { "latencyMs": 123 }`, and
 *    `executionLedger: { "mode": "forensic", "elapsedMs": 1234,
 *      "terminalReason": "deadline" | "cancelled" | "provider_exhausted" | "completed",
 *      "providers": ["groq"], "models": ["..."], "counts": { "model": 1, "tool": 2 } }`,
 *    `execution: { "iterations": 24, "maxIterations": 24, "toolCalls": 35,
 *   "prefetchToolCalls": 8, "loopToolCalls": 27,
 *   "stopReason": "response" | "iteration_budget" | "soft_limit" | "repeated_tool_call" | "empty_response" | "provider_timeout",
 *     "synthesisStarted": true, "recoveryStarted": false,
 *     "diagnosticCodes": ["..."],
 *      "diagnosticDetails"?: ["bounded contract violation"],
 *      "evidenceConsistent"?: true | false }`, and
 *  `_meta.rootPathFallback: { "used": true, "original": "..." }`.
 *  `execution.evidenceConsistent` (EI-012) is true when this turn's
 *  run-ledger telemetry reconciled with its cited evidence, and
 *  false/absent when the reconciliation gate blocked the verdict.
 *  Error events expose only bounded failure metadata; provider context,
 *  raw model output, and runtime diagnostics are never part of the client contract.
 * @summary Send a message to the AI assistant (SSE streaming)
 */
